From 01b72cc65106336e0da641870b892cfe7088a2e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Shaun Adams <s.adams@f5.com>
Date: Sun, 14 Jun 2026 17:46:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 20/42] transports+configstore: GET list, GET single, DELETE on
 /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/...
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Completes the read+delete half of the tenant-scoped provider admin so
the API is ergonomic for E2E provisioning + iteration (no DB-direct
mutation needed to retry an experiment). PUT/update is deferred — the
legacy UpdateProvider's key-cascade + VKPC-resync logic is large
enough to warrant its own patch.

configstore additions:
- ConfigStore.GetProviderConfigByTenant(ctx, tenantID, provider) matches
  on (tenant_id, name). Composite uniqueness from patch 0006 makes the
  lookup deterministic; the existing GetProviderConfig is refactored to
  delegate through a shared getProviderConfigInternal.
- ConfigStore.DeleteProviderForTenant(ctx, tenantID, provider) only
  removes the row whose (tenant_id, name) matches; returns ErrNotFound
  when the provider exists in another tenant. Existing DeleteProvider
  now scopes through DefaultTenantID for safety so multi-tenant data
  can't be wrong-deleted via the legacy single-tenant call shape.
- MockConfigStore updated.
- Tests cover: cross-tenant isolation of GET single + ErrNotFound when
  the provider lives in a different tenant's scope, DELETE removing
  only the calling tenant's row, DELETE returning ErrNotFound for
  cross-tenant attempts.

Transport additions:
- handlers.TenantProviderHandler gains listProviders (GET list),
  getProvider (GET single), deleteProvider (DELETE). DELETE evicts the
  per-tenant runtime so the next inference request lazy-loads with
  the provider removed; redacted reads use ProviderConfig.Redacted()
  so key values don't leak to admin UIs.
- Handler tests cover: list filter by tenant, GET single 404 when the
  provider exists only in another tenant, DELETE happy path + evict,
  DELETE 404 when nothing matches.

Layer 1 integration test extended with a Phase 4 — delete acme's
openai via the route, confirm acme's list drops, globex's openai
survives, and the deleted-provider GET returns 404 (not globex's row,
the critical cross-tenant safety check).

Out of scope (separate patch): PUT /api/tenants/{tid}/providers/{provider}
update. Needs a tenant-scoped variant of UpdateProvider that wraps the
existing key-cascade + VKPC-resync logic with a tenant_id filter on
the row lookup; non-trivial enough to deserve its own review pass.

Ref: https://jira.f5net.com/browse/XC-25496
